From ed08620476dfc343f92f59b7c159391c07af1c61 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 15:48:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] config/db/seeds.rb: seed a baseline "og_plus" Model row

Upstream removed local model seeding (4321bceb, "No longer necessary
now that we can delegate to the model poller and synchronizer") --
that poller/synchronizer syncs model definitions from trmnl.com's own
hosted API. This qemu boot-test environment has no route to that API,
so without at least one Model row, POST /api/setup's device
provisioning always fails here: Devices::Provisioner#create looks up
model_id via Repositories::Model#find_by(name:), and device.model_id
has been NOT NULL since migration 20260126141642, so a nil lookup is a
hard NotNullConstraintError, not a soft default.

Name is "og_plus", not "og": Aspects::Firmware::Headers::Transformers::
ModelName remaps every real device's HTTP_MODEL header ("og" included,
and any unrecognized name too, via its own fallback) to one of a small
canonical set before the lookup ever runs -- "og" maps to "og_plus",
so a row literally named "og" is never actually matched by any real
request. Confirmed live: seeding "og" left the Model row genuinely
present in postgres but /api/setup still 404s with a model_id NOT NULL
violation, because the app looks up "og_plus", not "og".

A real deployment with real internet access can still let the poller
sync/replace this later (find_or_create only inserts if "og_plus"
doesn't already exist); this seed just keeps first boot testable
without depending on that sync. 800x480 is the real TRMNL OG e-ink
resolution.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [oe-specific -- this qemu boot-test
environment has no route to trmnl.com's model poller/synchronizer that
upstream now relies on instead of a local seed]

Signed-off-by: Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>
---
 config/db/seeds.rb | 26 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+)

diff --git a/config/db/seeds.rb b/config/db/seeds.rb
index 972ed098..23a8ad36 100644
--- a/config/db/seeds.rb
+++ b/config/db/seeds.rb
@@ -8,3 +8,29 @@ Hanami.app["db.gateway"]
         {id: 2, name: "Verified"},
         {id: 3, name: "Closed"}
       ]
+
+# Upstream removed local model seeding (4321bceb, "No longer necessary
+# now that we can delegate to the model poller and synchronizer") --
+# that poller/synchronizer syncs model definitions from trmnl.com's own
+# hosted API. This qemu boot-test environment has no route to that API,
+# so without at least one Model row, POST /api/setup's device
+# provisioning always fails here: Devices::Provisioner#create looks up
+# model_id via Repositories::Model#find_by(name:), and `device.model_id`
+# has been NOT NULL since migration 20260126141642, so a nil lookup is a
+# hard NotNullConstraintError, not a soft default. Name is "og_plus", not
+# "og": Aspects::Firmware::Headers::Transformers::ModelName remaps every
+# real device's HTTP_MODEL header ("og" included, and any unrecognized
+# name too, via its own fallback) to one of a small canonical set before
+# the lookup ever runs -- "og" maps to "og_plus", so a row literally named
+# "og" is never actually matched by any real request. A real deployment
+# with real internet access can still let the poller sync/replace this
+# later (find_or_create only inserts if "og_plus" doesn't already exist);
+# this seed just keeps first boot testable without depending on that
+# sync. 800x480 is the real TRMNL OG e-ink resolution.
+Hanami.app["repositories.model"].find_or_create(
+  name: "og_plus",
+  label: "OG",
+  description: "The original TRMNL e-ink display.",
+  width: 800,
+  height: 480
+)
